{title: 091 - Ye Watchers and Ye Holy Ones}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #091 • LASST UNS ERFREUEN (WITH ALLELUIAS) • 9.9.7.10.8}
{lyricist: Athelstan Riley}
{composer: Geistliche Kirchengesange, Koln}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 91}
{meta: tune LASST UNS ERFREUEN (WITH ALLELUIAS)}
{meta: meter 9.9.7.10.8}
{meta: category God the Father - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Cm/G]Ye watchers [Eb]and [Cm]ye [Fm]holy [Eb/Bb]ones,
[Eb/Bb]Bright seraphs, [Bb]cherubim [Cm/Eb]and [Eb]thrones,
[Bb]Raise [F/A]the [Bb]glad [Eb]strain, [Fm]Alleluia!
[Cm]Cry [Bb7]out, [Ab]dominions, [Bb/F]princedoms, powers,
[Fm/C]Virtues, archangels, [Eb/Bb]angels' [Bb7/Ab]choirs:
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Cm/G]Alleluia! [F/A]Alleluia!
[Cm/G]Alleluia! [Ab]Alleluia!
[Cm/G]Alleluia!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Cm/G]O higher [Eb]than [Fm]the [Bb]cherubim,
[Eb/Bb]More glorious [Bb]than [Eb]the [Cm/Eb]seraphim,
[Bb]Lead [F/A]their [Bb]praises, [Fm]Alleluia!
[Cm]Thou [Eb/Bb]bearer of [Bb/F]th'eternal Word,
[Fm/C]Most [Cm]gracious, [Bb]magnify [Fm/C]the [Bb7/Ab]Lord.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Cm/G]O friends, [Eb/Bb]in gladness [Bb]let [Eb/Bb]us sing,
[Eb/Bb]Supernal [Bb]anthems [Ab/Eb]echoing,
[Bb]Alleluia! [Eb]Alleluia!
[Cm]To [Eb/Bb]God [Bb/F]the [Eb/Bb]Father, [Ab/Eb]God [Fm/C]the [Bb/F]Son,
[Fm/C]And [Cm]God [Fm/C]the [Bb]Spirit, [Eb/Bb]Three [Fm/C]in [Bb7/Ab]One.
{end_of_verse}
